## Brief Overview

---

To organize a congress in Malaga, fix the dates, the number of delegates and the program first, then choose the venue, then the hotels, and only then write the audiovisual brief for your supplier. Malaga Event Gear supplies the sound, the display or the projector, the microphones and the technician, from the [MICE Pack](/packages/mice/) for up to 120 guests. The venue, the hotels, interpretation and the rest of the event go through the venue, the Malaga Convention Bureau, an agency and our partners.

## Key Highlights

---

-   Decide in this order: dates, delegates and program, venue, accommodation, audiovisual brief.
-   The Malaga Convention Bureau lists technical advice for organizing congresses, venue and hotel availability and local logistics among the requests it answers.
-   We supply the audiovisual side: sound, a display or a projector, microphones and a technician. We are not a venue, a DMC or an organizer.
-   Interpretation equipment is not in our own inventory. We coordinate it with a subcontracted partner.
-   Our bookings need at least 24 hours of notice, and a congress needs the brief as early as your dates are set.

-   **Who delivers it?** Our crew delivers, installs and tests the equipment. We work delivery only, with no self pickup.
-   **Who handles hotels?** Our partner Top Group Express, for group bookings.
-   **What is not covered?** The venue, catering, registration, accommodation and equipment outside our own inventory.

## Start With Dates, Delegates and Program

Everything else depends on three facts, so write them down first.

-   **Dates.** Venues and hotels are booked against dates, so a congress with flexible dates has more choice than one with fixed ones.
-   **Delegates.** The number of delegates decides the room. A report prepared for the [Malaga Convention Bureau](https://sto.malaga.eu/export/sites/sto-malaga/.galleries/Documentos-Memorias/MEMORIA-2024-MCB.pdf) puts the average congress in Malaga in 2024 at more than 300 delegates, which is a useful reference when you size yours.
-   **Program.** One plenary room is a different brief from a plenary plus several parallel sessions, because every room needs its own sound, microphones and display.

## Choose the Venue

The usual choices are a congress center, a hotel with meeting rooms or a mix of both. In Malaga, [FYCMA](https://fycma.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Informe-de-Sostenibilidad-Fycma-2025.pdf), the city's trade fair and congress center, lists an auditorium for up to 900 people and another for 600. The Torremolinos and Marbella congress palaces and the hotels of the Costa del Sol are the other names organizers use. Our post on [MICE events in Malaga](/blog/mice-events-in-malaga/) lists the main venues with their own capacity figures.

Whichever you choose, confirm the capacity for your layout, because a room holds fewer people with tables than in rows. Ask what equipment is included, as covered below.

## Book Accommodation for Delegates

A report prepared for the Convention Bureau found that 69.7% of the people attending meetings in Malaga in 2024 came from outside the province, so most of your delegates will need rooms. Book them once the dates and the venue are fixed, because the distance from the hotel to the venue is part of the choice.

For group bookings, our partner [Top Group Express](https://topgroupexpress.com/en) has years of experience reserving hotels for groups, working with the agencies, DMCs and companies that organize a delegation's travel. We handle the sound and the screens, they handle the rooms.

