## Where We Deliver and How to Book

We are based in Malaga and deliver across the Costa del Sol: Marbella, Fuengirola, Torremolinos, Benalmadena, Estepona, Mijas, Ronda and Nerja are all in our service area, and we also serve Sevilla with no minimum order. Granada needs a booking over 400 euros to cover the single day travel.

We work delivery only, with no self pickup, and every booking needs at least 24 hours of notice. [Contact us](/contact/) with your venue, your dates and the number of delegates, and see the wider picture in our guide to [MICE events in Malaga](/blog/mice-events-in-malaga/). If your congress is held in a hotel, our guide to [hotel in house AV vs independent AV supplier](/blog/hotel-in-house-av-vs-independent-av-supplier/) explains how to choose who provides the audiovisual side.

## Conclusion

To organize a congress in Malaga, work in this order: dates, delegates and program, venue, accommodation and then the audiovisual brief. The Malaga Convention Bureau, the venue and an agency cover most of the steps before the last one. We cover the audiovisual part, from the MICE Pack at 490 euros ex VAT, and we coordinate interpretation with a partner. [Contact us](/contact/) with your event details, or see the rest of what we offer on our [event technology service](/blog/event-technology-service/) page.

## FAQs

### Where do I start to organize a congress in Malaga?

With the dates, the number of delegates and the program, because the venue, the hotels and the technical side all depend on them. Then choose the venue and book the hotels. The Malaga Convention Bureau lists technical advice for organizing congresses, venue and hotel availability and local logistics among the requests it answers. The audiovisual brief comes last, and [we can help with it](/contact/).

### Do I need a destination management company?

It depends on how much of the logistics you want to hand over. A destination management company or an agency can handle transport, the social program and the group's logistics. We are not one: we supply the audiovisual equipment and a technician, and we work with whichever agency or organizer you use.

### What audiovisual equipment does a congress room need?

At least a sound system, microphones for the speakers and for questions from the floor, and a display or a projector. Some congresses add a lectern or a stage platform. A technician runs the sound and the microphones, and a multilingual congress needs interpretation equipment, which we coordinate with a subcontracted partner. The [MICE Pack](/packages/mice/) covers a room of up to 120 guests.

### How far in advance should I book the audiovisual side?

Our bookings need at least 24 hours of notice, but a congress should not wait for that. The venue and the hotels are booked against your dates, so send us the brief as soon as the venue and the program are fixed, and we tell you plainly what we can supply and what we would source. We do not promise availability until we have checked.

### What audiovisual setup does a medical congress in Malaga usually need?

The same core as any other congress room: a sound system, microphones for the speakers and for questions from the floor, and a display or projector the whole room can read. The [MICE Pack](/packages/mice/) covers that from our own inventory, with active speakers, a 60 inch LED display, a gooseneck and a wireless handheld microphone and a technician. The technician operates the sound and the microphones and fixes a failing screen or projector, while each speaker runs their own slides. Simultaneous interpretation and interactive voting are not in our own inventory. We coordinate them with a subcontracted partner, so tell us what you need and we look for a solution with our suppliers, if there is one.
